//CLOVERLEAF - 1500mo//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/TB#BELTC.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Girdle"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Girdles are generally similar to belts. Unlike belts, girdles are not used to hold up pants and dungarees, but to carry pouches, scabbards, and the like. 

STATISTICS:

Weight: 2"

	SAY NAME2 "Cloverleaf"
	SAY DESC "This vibrant cloth belt is woven with dried four-leaf clovers, a traditional symbol of good fortune among halfling communities. It was originally crafted by a gentle halfling elder from the Gullykin village to protect a young, reckless explorer heading into the wilderness. Legends say that while wearing it, the youth narrowly avoided rampaging ankhegs and survived several lethal traps by sheer, unexplained coincidence.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Luck: +1

Weight: 2"



//GOLDEN GIRDLE OF URNST - 1500mo//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/BELT02.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Girdle"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Girdles are generally similar to belts. Unlike belts, girdles are not used to hold up pants and dungarees, but to carry pouches, scabbards, and the like. 

STATISTICS:

Weight: 2"

	SAY NAME2 "Golden Girdle of Urnst"
	SAY DESC "Created to protect a powerful wizard against malevolent warriors, this magical garment is made of red silk strewn with golden flakes. It is enchanted to give protection against slashing weapons of any type.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Armor Class: +4 vs. slashing attacks

Weight: 2"



//GIRDLE OF BLUNTNESS - 1500mo//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/BELT03.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Girdle"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Girdles are generally similar to belts. Unlike belts, girdles are not used to hold up pants and dungarees, but to carry pouches, scabbards, and the like. 

STATISTICS:

Weight: 2"

	SAY NAME2 "Girdle of Bluntness"
	SAY DESC "Having lost friends and loved ones to a series of raids by hill giants, Garrar the Powerful made it his mission to cleanse his homeland of their presence. It is not known where he acquired this item, but with it he single-handedly dispatched dozens of the creatures, all the while protected from the blows of their clubs. The remaining giants fled to neighboring lands—lands that lacked a similar champion and did not fare as well.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Armor Class: +4 vs. crushing attacks

Weight: 2"





//GIRDLE OF PIERCING - 1500mo//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/BELT04.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Girdle"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Girdles are generally similar to belts. Unlike belts, girdles are not used to hold up pants and dungarees, but to carry pouches, scabbards, and the like. 

STATISTICS:

Weight: 2"

	SAY NAME2 "Girdle of Piercing"
	SAY DESC "An infamous highwayman in his day, Pandar of Scardale made quite a name for himself vexing the elves of Cormanthor forest. To their annoyance, he continually used the wood to escape the law—and with the aid of this girdle, the elves' arrows as well. Unfortunately for Pandar, pit traps and starvation proved a slower, but effective, substitution.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Armor Class: +3 vs. missile and piercing attacks

Weight: 2"





//BELT OF THE CUNNING ROGUE - 1800mo - solo ladri//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/BDBELT03.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Girdle"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Girdles are generally similar to belts. Unlike belts, girdles are not used to hold up pants and dungarees, but to carry pouches, scabbards, and the like. 

STATISTICS:

Weight: 2"

	SAY NAME2 "Belt of the Cunning Rogue"
	SAY DESC "This dark, oiled leather belt was crafted by a master dungeon delver who specialized in bypassing ancient defenses. It originally belonged to a notorious rogue famous for infiltrating lethal elven ruins and untying the most complex wire triggers. The heavy buckle conceals a secret compartment filled with specialized tension picks and delicate counter-weights, allowing a skilled thief to work safely in the shadows.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Disarm Traps: +15%
- Set Traps: +15%

Weight: 2"




//GIRDLE OF THE UNYIELDING FORM - 3500mo//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/TB#BELTM.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Girdle"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Girdles are generally similar to belts. Unlike belts, girdles are not used to hold up pants and dungarees, but to carry pouches, scabbards, and the like. 

STATISTICS:

Weight: 2"

	SAY NAME2 "Girdle of the Unyielding Form"
	SAY DESC "This thick leather girdle was forged in the deep caverns of the Underdark, commissioned by a duergar king who feared the petrifying gaze of basilisk infestations. Woven into the iron-reinforced seams are crushed shards of iron golem cores and residual magic from an antimagic eye. The wearer feels an unnatural density settling into their bones, making their physical shape completely immutable to hostile magic while simultaneously unweaving minor spells targeted at them.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Save vs. Transmutation: +4
- Magic Resistance: +5%

Weight: 2"







//GIRDLE OF HILL GIANT STRENGTH - solo combattenti - 10000mo//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/BELT06.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Girdle"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Girdles are generally similar to belts. Unlike belts, girdles are not used to hold up pants and dungarees, but to carry pouches, scabbards, and the like. 

STATISTICS:

Weight: 2"

	SAY NAME2 "Girdle of Hill Giant Strength"
	SAY DESC "Forged from crude iron and thick, reinforced leather, this heavy belt radiates the brute force of the foothills. It channels the primal, unyielding power of the hill giants, flooding the wearer's muscles with immense physical strength. While lacking the elemental protections of its more powerful counterparts, the artifact ensures its user can easily crush rock and bone alike through sheer, overwhelming muscle.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Strength: 19

Weight: 2"




//GIRDLE OF STONE GIANT STRENGTH - solo combattenti - 12000mo//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/BELT07.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Girdle"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Girdles are generally similar to belts. Unlike belts, girdles are not used to hold up pants and dungarees, but to carry pouches, scabbards, and the like. 

STATISTICS:

Weight: 2"

	SAY NAME2 "Girdle of Stone Giant Strength"
	SAY DESC "Carved from deep-mountain basalt and bound in heavy iron, this solid belt carries the tectonic weight of the peaks. It infuses the wearer with the monolithic power of the stone giants, granting the muscle needed to shatter boulders with bare hands. Imbued with the mountain's stubborn nature, the artifact grounds the user, turning their skin as resilient as bedrock to deflect oncoming weapons.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Strength: 19
- Physical Damage Resistance: +5%

Weight: 2"




//GIRDLE OF FROST GIANT STRENGTH - solo combattenti - 12000mo//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/BELT08.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Girdle"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Girdles are generally similar to belts. Unlike belts, girdles are not used to hold up pants and dungarees, but to carry pouches, scabbards, and the like. 

STATISTICS:

Weight: 2"

	SAY NAME2 "Girdle of Frost Giant Strength"
	SAY DESC "Forged from frozen iron and ice-drake hide, this massive belt radiates the raw power of the Great Glacier. It directly channels the legendary might of the frost giants, surging through the wearer's veins to grant colossal physical strength. The heavy enchantments layered within the material also act as a shield, hardening the flesh against crushing weapons and creating a dense barrier against absolute zero temperatures.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Strength: 20
- Physical Resistance: +5%
- Cold Resistance: +20%

