	SAY NAME1 "Girdle"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Girdles are generally similar to belts. Unlike belts, girdles are not used to hold up pants and dungarees, but to carry pouches, scabbards, and the like. 

STATISTICS:

Weight: 2"

	SAY NAME2 "Girdle of Fortitude"
	SAY DESC "This girdle greatly increases the wearer's Constitution. King Violos used it when leading an expedition against marsh trolls. He'd been severely sickened the past winter and was no longer the healthy man he once was. The belt gave extra years to his life and inspired his men to renew their confidence in their king once more.

STATISTICS:

Charge abilities:
Equipped abilities:
– Constitution: 18

Weight: 2"







//BELT OF THE SKILLFUL BLADE - solo spadaccini - 11000mo//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/BDBELT02.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Girdle"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Girdles are generally similar to belts. Unlike belts, girdles are not used to hold up pants and dungarees, but to carry pouches, scabbards, and the like. 

STATISTICS:

Weight: 2"

	SAY NAME2 "Belt of the Skillful Blade"
	SAY DESC "A blacksmith in Cormyr is responsible for designing this item. Say'an Keenedge was renowned for designing the sharpest, best balanced, and most beautiful blades in the country. She was also a bit of a hothead and grew furious when she saw less-skilled fighters wielding her weapons. For her finest work she handed out one of these belts free with purchase, in order that her weapons never be mishandled.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- 1/2 extra attack per round
– THAC0 with the off hand: +2
– Slashing Damage: +10%
- Piercing Damage: +10%
- Armor Class vs. Slashing: +2
- Armor Class vs. Piercing: +2

Weight: 2"




//GIRDLE OF ABSORPTION  - 2500mo//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/BDBELT04.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Girdle"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Girdles are generally similar to belts. Unlike belts, girdles are not used to hold up pants and dungarees, but to carry pouches, scabbards, and the like. 

STATISTICS:

Weight: 2"

	SAY NAME2 "Girdle of Absorption"
	SAY DESC "This peculiar girdle was commissioned centuries ago by a cautious archmage weary of falling victim to rival spellcasters. The supple leather is intricately woven with silver threads and etched with shimmering abjuration runes. When struck by hostile arcane energy, these runes flare to life, drawing the brunt of the destructive force into the belt's enchanted weave before it can harm the wearer.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Magical Damage Resistance: +40%

Weight: 2"






//GIRDLE OF INERTIAL BARRIER - 6500mo//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/BELT10.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Girdle"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Girdles are generally similar to belts. Unlike belts, girdles are not used to hold up pants and dungarees, but to carry pouches, scabbards, and the like. 

STATISTICS:

Weight: 2"

	SAY NAME2 "Girdle of Inertial Barrier"
	SAY DESC "When worn, this belt creates a dense curtain of air around the wearer. This curtain or barrier provides superior protection against breath attacks. By the scorch marks on the worn leather, it is obvious that this belt has been worn at least once against a dragon.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Save vs. Breath: +4
- Immunity to Wing Buffet, Sleep and Unconsciousness

Weight: 2"







//GIRDLE OF AVOIDANCE - 9000mo//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/OHRBELT2.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Girdle"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Girdles are generally similar to belts. Unlike belts, girdles are not used to hold up pants and dungarees, but to carry pouches, scabbards, and the like. 

STATISTICS:

Weight: 2"

	SAY NAME2 "Girdle of Avoidance"
	SAY DESC "Crafted during the Time of Troubles by Malakor, a paranoid wizard of Mystra, this leather girdle was designed purely for survival. Obsessed with the fear of assassination, Malakor wove shifting illusionary magic into the leather. When the wearer is struck, the belt releases a distortionary pulse, causing the user's form to blur wildly. Though Malakor was eventually poisoned—a threat the belt could not prevent—his creation remains highly sought-after by adventurers.

STATISTICS:

Combat abilities:
– 10% chance when hit to cast Blur on wearer

Weight: 2"








